<http://data.silknow.org/object/79346758-17a3-3d32-be3e-0ab30bb4d9b1/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Textile panel of woven silk. Woven with a floral pattern in orange on a white ground. The design consists of a meandering floral stem with at least three varieties of flower. There are small leaves and berries on the stems.\n\nTissue has a tabby ground and the pattern is bound in 3/1 twill by a separate white binding warp. The warp has 4 ground warp threads, and one binding warp thread. The weft has one ground and one pattern weft.\n\nOn the left hand side there is a selvedge, 7 cords woven in tabby, and the two inner with the ground weft only, the 5 outer cords with the ground and pattern weft used together."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/79346758-17a3-3d32-be3e-0ab30bb4d9b1> .

