        rdfs:comment                   "Textile panel of woven silk. Woven with a floral pattern in orange on a white ground. The design consists of a meandering floral stem with at least three varieties of flower. There are small leaves and berries on the stems.\n\nTissue has a tabby ground and the pattern is bound in 3/1 twill by a separate white binding warp. The warp has 4 ground warp threads, and one binding warp thread. The weft has one ground and one pattern weft.\n\nOn the left hand side there is a selvedge, 7 cords woven in tabby, and the two inner with the ground weft only, the 5 outer cords with the ground and pattern weft used together."@en , "Textile panel of woven silk, France, 1750-1775"@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/1163b6a4-ddaa-3889-b498-663ec0feb215> ;
